            "rationale": "This total-function equation defines rightTriangle(A, B, C) by unfolding it to positivity checks and the three possible Pythagorean equalities; it is the mathematical summary used by the specification, not an additional fact about that summary.",
            "source_rule_id": "rule-d1a23396f61dd26b11833b39066cbd64b498e0dfb07eaea1e6c090daaa0b0893",
            "start_line": 8,
            "text": "  rule rightTriangle(A, B, C)\n       => (A >Int 0)\n          andBool (B >Int 0)\n          andBool (C >Int 0)\n          andBool (((A *Int A) +Int (B *Int B)) ==Int (C *Int C)\n                   orBool ((A *Int A) +Int (C *Int C)) ==Int (B *Int B)\n                   orBool ((B *Int B) +Int (C *Int C)) ==Int (A *Int A))"
        },
        {
            "attributes": [],
            "classification": "DEFINITION",
